<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 3.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 3.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 01/03/97  12/27/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    154.11    163.43    66.27	70.28     51.50</p>
<p>West	    133.60    150.19    51.56	56.71     60.30</p>
<p>Total Canada  287.72    313.61    58.52	63.05     56.20</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 01/03/97: 232.55 bcf, 12/27/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 01/03/97: 259.11 bcf, 12/27/96: 264.84 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. ((--Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
